
# .cursor/rules/security.mdc

## Rule: Never Log Sensitive Data
- Do not log passwords, tokens, connection strings or personal data.
- Redact or exclude sensitive fields in logs and exceptions.

## Rule: Validate Input
- Always validate model inputs using [Required], [StringLength], [Range], etc.
- Use FluentValidation or custom filters for complex scenarios.

## Rule: Protect Against Injection
- Use parameterized queries with EF Core to prevent SQL injection.
- Do not allow raw SQL queries unless absolutely necessary.

## Rule: HTTPS Only
- Ensure redirection to HTTPS is enabled and enforced via middleware.

## Rule: Secure Headers
- If modifying HTTP headers, include security headers like `X-Content-Type-Options`, `X-Frame-Options`, etc.
